** interface of the WebGPU API is used to record the results of queries on passes, such as occlusion or timestamp queries.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6103,"content":" * The **`GPURenderBundle`** interface of the WebGPU API represents a container for pre-recorded bundles of commands.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6117,"content":" * The **`GPURenderBundleEncoder`** interface of the WebGPU API is used to pre-record bundles of commands.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6124,"content":"     * The **`finish()`** method of the GPURenderBundleEncoder interface completes recording of the current render bundle command sequence, returning a GPURenderBundle object that can be passed into a GPURenderPassEncoder.executeBundles() call to execute those commands in a specific render pass.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6167,"content":"     * The **`end()`** method of the GPURenderPassEncoder interface completes recording of the current render pass command sequence.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6179,"content":"     * The **`executeBundles()`** method of the GPURenderPassEncoder interface executes commands previously recorded into the referenced GPURenderBundles, as part of this render pass.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6534,"content":" * The **`IDBCursor`** interface of the IndexedDB API represents a cursor for traversing or iterating over multiple records in a database.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6546,"content":"     * The **`key`** read-only property of the IDBCursor interface returns the key for the record at the cursor's position. If the cursor is outside its range, this is set to undefined. The cursor's key can be any data type.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6588,"content":"     * The **`delete()`** method of the IDBCursor interface returns an IDBRequest object, and, in a separate thread, deletes the record at the cursor's position, without changing the cursor's position. Once the record is deleted, the cursor's value is set to null.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6594,"content":"     * The **`update()`** method of the IDBCursor interface returns an IDBRequest object, and, in a separate thread, updates the value at the current position of the cursor in the object store. If the cursor points to a record that has just been deleted, a new record is created.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6607,"content":" * The **`IDBCursorWithValue`** interface of the IndexedDB API represents a cursor for traversing or iterating over multiple records in a database. It is the same as the IDBCursor, except that it includes the value property.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6736,"content":" * **`IDBIndex`** interface of the IndexedDB API provides asynchronous access to an index in a database. An index is a kind of object store for looking up records in another object store, called the referenced object store. You use this interface to retrieve data.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6772,"content":"     * The **`count()`** method of the IDBIndex interface returns an IDBRequest object, and in a separate thread, returns the number of records within a key range.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6924,"content":"     * The **`add()`** method of the IDBObjectStore interface returns an IDBRequest object, and, in a separate thread, creates a structured clone of the value, and stores the cloned value in the object store. This is for adding new records to an object store.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6936,"content":"     * The **`count()`** method of the IDBObjectStore interface returns an IDBRequest object, and, in a separate thread, returns the total number of records that match the provided key or IDBKeyRange. If no arguments are provided, it returns the total number of records in the store.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6942,"content":"     * The **`createIndex()`** method of the IDBObjectStore interface creates and returns a new IDBIndex object in the connected database. It creates a new field/column defining a new data point for each database record to contain.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6948,"content":"     * The **`delete()`** method of the IDBObjectStore interface returns an IDBRequest object, and, in a separate thread, deletes the specified record or records.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6960,"content":"     * The **`get()`** method of the IDBObjectStore interface returns an IDBRequest object, and, in a separate thread, returns the object selected by the specified key. This is for retrieving specific records from an object store.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6972,"content":"     * The **`getAllKeys()`** method of the IDBObjectStore interface returns an IDBRequest object retrieves record keys for all objects in the object store matching the specified parameter or all objects in the store if no parameters are given.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6978,"content":"     * The **`getKey()`** method of the IDBObjectStore interface returns an IDBRequest object, and, in a separate thread, returns the key selected by the specified query. This is for retrieving specific records from an object store.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":6984,"content":"     * The **`index()`** method of the IDBObjectStore interface opens a named index in the current object store, after which it can be used to, for example, return a series of records sorted by that index using a cursor.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":7002,"content":"     * The **`put()`** method of the IDBObjectStore interface updates a given record in a database, or inserts a new record if the given item does not already exist.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":7440,"content":" * The **`Lock`** interface of the Web Locks API provides the name and mode of a lock. This may be a newly requested lock that is received in the callback to LockManager.request(), or a record of an active or queued lock returned by LockManager.query().","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":8271,"content":"     * The read-only **`startTime`** property returns the first timestamp recorded for this PerformanceEntry. The meaning of this property depends on the value of this entry's entryType.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":8328,"content":" * The **`PerformanceObserver`** interface is used to observe performance measurement events and be notified of new performance entries as they are recorded in the browser's performance timeline.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":9242,"content":" * The **`ReadableStreamBYOBRequest`** interface of the Streams API represents a \"pull request\" for data from an underlying source that will made as a zero-copy transfer to a consumer (bypassing the stream's internal queues).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":14752,"content":"    /** The **`console.timeStamp()`** static method adds a single marker to the browser's Performance tool (Firefox bug 1387528, Chrome). This lets you correlate a point in your code with the other events recorded in the timeline, such as layout and paint events. */","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":15150,"content":"type MediaEncodingType = \"record\" | \"webrtc\";","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":15324,"content":"     * The **`executeBundles()`** method of